<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yeshaq I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1414">1414</a>–<a href="/years/1429">1429</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yeshaq I was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> from 1414 to 1429, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawit-i">Dawit I</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomonic-dynasty">Solomonic dynasty</a>. He fought the Muslim states to the east, and some accounts place the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saad-ad-din-ii">Sa'ad ad-Din II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifat-sultanate">Ifat</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeila">Zeila</a> in his reign. He also sought allies abroad, sending an embassy to Alfonso V of Aragon in 1427.</p></div>
